## Printed
heading: FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLES
number: No 32
credit: Today's cross-word, the thirty-second in FUN'S series, was sent in by William Callander of Pulaski street, Brooklyn. He writes as follows: "The solving of your cross-word puzzles has been a source of keen delight not only to myself but to various members of my family and friends; but, hard as some of the puzzles have been to solve, I find it much more of a task to construct one."
instructions: Fill in the small squares with words corersponding to the list of clues and definitions given below. The solution to this puzzle will be published in next week's FUN.
solution heading: Solution to last week's cross-word puzzle.


